course: dictionary
lesson: 15068
title: Rhythmically
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rhythm is a steady pattern of beats, like a clock ticking or a drum going boom, boom, boom. When something happens rhythmically, it happens in that regular pattern. «The children clapped rhythmically to the song.» They clapped with a steady beat, one clap after another at even times.
explain: Rhythmically is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done. Find the action word first, such as clapped, marched or danced, then ask how it was done. Rhythmically answers that question. «The soldiers marched rhythmically across the field» means they marched with a steady beat, step after step.
explain: The word also works in music and poetry. A poem can have a steady beat, so we say its lines move rhythmically. Your heart beats rhythmically too, in a regular pattern. Next time you rest your hand on your chest, feel for it.
fact: Rhythm is a regular pattern of beats or sounds.
fact: «Rhythmically» means with a regular, repeated beat or pattern.
fact: «Rhythmically» can also mean in a way that has to do with rhythm in music or poetry.
fact: Children can clap, march or dance rhythmically in music and PE lessons.
fact: «Rhythmic» and «rhythm» are in the same word family as «rhythmically».
exercise: «The drummer tapped the sticks rhythmically.» What does rhythmically mean here? | Without any sound at all | *With a steady, repeated beat | Very slowly and quietly | Very loudly and angrily
exercise: «The children clapped rhythmically.» Find and copy the word that tells how they clapped. | children | clapped | *rhythmically | the
exercise: What does a poem need to move rhythmically? | *A steady beat, like the rhythm of a song | Pictures on every page | Lines that all have no pattern at all | Only very long words
test: «The waves hit the beach rhythmically, one after another.» What does rhythmically mean? | Far away from the sea | Only once and then never again | *In a regular, repeated pattern | Very fast and out of control
test: «Ella was asked to breathe rhythmically while she rested.» What is Ella doing? | Breathing very fast and then stopping | Holding her breath until she goes red | *Breathing in a steady, regular pattern | Coughing loudly
exam: Which answer best explains rhythmically in a music lesson? | *In a way that keeps a steady beat | In a way that is very sad and slow | In a way that has no sound at all | In a way that is hidden from everyone
